INSERT [dbo].[ContactUs] ([Id], [Name], [Email], [Subject], [ContactDate]) VALUES (6752, N'Erik Bourget', N'erikb@easytaxcredit.org', N'Dear Business Owner,
 (if you are NOT the business owner, please forward this email to whom it may concern)

Has COVID-19 affected your business in big ways or small?
Do you have any employees?

If you answered YES to these questions and your business is located in the USA, you may be qualified to receive the "Employee Retention Tax Credit" (ERTC in short).  ERTC is NOT a loan, and you DON''T need to refund it!

By the way, this is NOT a spam email, and this is NOT a fraud.  The ERTC is a very real government assistance program that was part of the CARES Act of 2020.  The government has authorized unprecedented stimulus, and yet billions of dollars will go unclaimed.  In fact, a vast majority of businesses we’ve successfully gotten millions in funding for had no idea they were qualified to receive it!  You can claim ERTC even if you received Payroll Protection Program (PPP) funds.

The problem is, ERTC is complex and time-consuming. But what if I told you that there''s an easier way to claim your ERTC benefits?

My name is Erik and I would like to introduce you to ERTC Express – a powerful tool that simplifies the ERTC claims process, so you can get the benefits you deserve quickly and easily. ERTC Express helps you:

- Determine if you''re eligible for ERTC;
- Calculate the maximum amount of ERTC you can claim (up to $26,000 per employee);
- Complete the necessary forms and submit them to the IRS;
- Receive your ERTC refund QUICKLY.

So far we’ve helped over 10,000 businesses all over the country receive between $20,000 and $3,000,000 in just the past 12 months! Our team of CPAs is always available to answer your questions and help you navigate the ERTC claims process.

If you''re interested in learning more about how ERTC Express can help you claim your ERTC benefits hassle-free, I would invite you to visit our website and see if you qualify!  You can use our proprietary "QuickEstimate Calculator" to find out how much the IRS may owe you.

Click the link below to get the funding you deserve:
https://go.easytaxcredit.org/quick-estimate-calculator-us4
(you may scroll down a bit on the page to find the calculator)

Best regards,
Erik Bourget

11407 SW Amu Street, Suite #T7902
Tualatin, OR 97062
USA









This is my first and last message to you, but should you wish to unsubscribe anyway, you can do so by clicking the link below:
https://easytaxcredit.org/unsubscribe.php?d=mcqsprep.com', CAST(N'2023-02-24T12:10:18.233' AS DateTime))
